      "writtenOn": "2023-11-10T16:57:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "New proposition.\n\nIn this way, I think:\n- The framework just need to copy the value used internally, no need to do boring conversions.\n- The vendor can use the `const int` values listed, and the supported values for a given version of the interface is well defined.\n- It\u0027s well defined that it\u0027s a bitmask.\n\nWhich is less good:\n- The `const int` values are mapped to `enum` backed in `int32_t` in C++. You should need to cast each values to avoid compilation warning.\n- There is more opportunity to set unspecified values. But as this will come from the framework to the HAL, I think it\u0027s fine.\n\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "5e025564_4008b854",
      "revId": "d1744d3e132ec9e66be39b090b60de3e0fb16ac3",
